# 👥 HR Analytics – Employee Attrition Prediction

## Project Overview

This project analyzes employee data to identify key factors associated with employee attrition and develops a machine learning model to predict employees who may be at risk of leaving the organization.

## Objectives

- Predict employees who are likely to leave.
- Identify important factors associated with employee attrition.
- Provide interpretable insights to support HR decision-making.
- Create dashboards and visualizations to communicate findings.

## Tools & Technologies

- Python
- SQL
- Power BI
- Pandas
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
- Seaborn
- Scikit-learn
- SHAP

## Machine Learning Model

- Random Forest Classifier

## Key Insights

- Higher attrition was observed among Sales Representatives and younger, single employees.
- Overtime, lower income, and limited promotion opportunities were important factors associated with attrition.
- Female employees showed a higher resignation rate in the analyzed dataset.
- Sales and R&D departments showed comparatively higher employee turnover.

## Outcome

The project demonstrates how data analysis and machine learning can be used to identify employee attrition patterns and support proactive HR decision-making.
